load ../pinned-progressions.maude

--- Coverage: the progression completes -- region steps, clean exit, post
--- steps, terminal.
search [1] in WHIPPLESCRIPT-PINNED-PROGRESSION :
  init =>* workflowDone(f1) RESIDUAL:Cfg .

--- Coverage (THE pinning claim): the admission trigger is consumed mid-flight
--- and the progression STILL completes -- bindings are values, matching gates
--- only admission.
search [1] in WHIPPLESCRIPT-PINNED-PROGRESSION :
  init =>* trig(f1, consumed) workflowDone(f1) RESIDUAL:Cfg .

--- Coverage: the lapse arm is reachable -- a break before the region drains
--- routes to lapsed with the arm's commit stamped.
search [1] in WHIPPLESCRIPT-PINNED-PROGRESSION :
  init =>* region(f1, lapsed) lapseAt(f1, N:Cnt) RESIDUAL:Cfg .

--- Coverage (point of no return): a post-region step commits AFTER the break
--- in log order -- statements outside the region consult no condition.
search [1] in WHIPPLESCRIPT-PINNED-PROGRESSION :
  init =>* condBroken(M:Cnt) postAt(f1, N:Cnt) RESIDUAL:Cfg
  such that lt(M:Cnt, N:Cnt) .

--- Coverage (repair): the condition breaks and REPAIRS before any advancing
--- commit observed the broken window -- the progression completes with no
--- lapse. `workflowDone` requires `region(_, done)`, and lapsed never becomes
--- done, so this state PROVES no lapse occurred despite `brokeEver`.
search [1] in WHIPPLESCRIPT-PINNED-PROGRESSION :
  init =>* brokeEver workflowDone(f1) RESIDUAL:Cfg .

--- Coverage (re-admission, Decision 4): two DISTINCT firings -- fact identity
--- is admission identity -- each complete independently.
search [1] in WHIPPLESCRIPT-PINNED-PROGRESSION :
  init2 =>* workflowDone(f1) workflowDone(f2) RESIDUAL:Cfg .

--- Invariant (fate-at-commit): no region step ever commits while the
--- condition stands broken -- the stateful break stamp coexisting with a
--- LATER step stamp is unreachable (the check is atomic with the commit).
search [1] in WHIPPLESCRIPT-PINNED-PROGRESSION :
  init =>* condBroken(M:Cnt) stepAt(f1, N:Cnt) RESIDUAL:Cfg
  such that lt(M:Cnt, N:Cnt) .

--- Invariant (lapse exactly once per firing): two lapse commits of the SAME
--- firing are unreachable -- its region cell is consumed into lapsed.
search [1] in WHIPPLESCRIPT-PINNED-PROGRESSION :
  init =>* lapseAt(f1, M:Cnt) lapseAt(f1, N:Cnt) RESIDUAL:Cfg .

--- Invariant (no silent stall): no FINAL state strands an open region --
--- every progression ends done, lapsed, or terminal. The reactive bite below
--- proves this non-vacuous.
search [1] in WHIPPLESCRIPT-PINNED-PROGRESSION :
  init =>! region(f1, open(K:Cnt)) RESIDUAL:Cfg .

--- Invariant (lapse is terminal for the region): a lapsed firing never reads
--- as done -- the two exits are exclusive by construction.
search [1] in WHIPPLESCRIPT-PINNED-PROGRESSION :
  init =>* lapseAt(f1, N:Cnt) region(f1, done) RESIDUAL:Cfg .

--- Invariant (the region gates its point of no return): a post-region step
--- never commits while the region is still open -- [apply] requires done, and
--- done is only reached by draining every step under the condition.
search [1] in WHIPPLESCRIPT-PINNED-PROGRESSION :
  init =>* region(f1, open(K:Cnt)) postAt(f1, N:Cnt) RESIDUAL:Cfg .

--- Bite (today's semantics stall silently): under reactive re-derivation --
--- continuations require the trigger to still match and the guard to still
--- hold, no lapse rule -- a FINAL state with the region still open is
--- reachable: the silent stall observed live in manual ch. 15.
search [1] in WHIPPLESCRIPT-REACTIVE-PROGRESSION :
  init =>! region(f1, open(K:Cnt)) RESIDUAL:Cfg .

--- WS-303: independent continuation queries read the present population.
--- Coverage: removal changes exists from its true admission result to false.
search [1] in WHIPPLESCRIPT-LIVE-CONTINUATION-QUERY :
  qInit =>* qObserved(qExists, q0, false, original, N:Nat) REST:QCfg .
--- Coverage: the SAME removal changes empty from false to true.
search [1] in WHIPPLESCRIPT-LIVE-CONTINUATION-QUERY :
  qInit =>* qObserved(qEmpty, q0, true, original, N:Nat) REST:QCfg .
--- Coverage: addition changes count >= 2 from false to true; nonempty alone
--- would not distinguish the admission population of one from two.
search [1] in WHIPPLESCRIPT-LIVE-CONTINUATION-QUERY :
  qInit =>* qObserved(qCountAtLeastTwo, q2, true, original, N:Nat) REST:QCfg .
--- Coverage: trigger consumption preserves the payload and all three query
--- observations occur after consumption and after the independent query
--- population has become empty. Retained clocks prove both orderings.
search [1] in WHIPPLESCRIPT-LIVE-CONTINUATION-QUERY :
  qInit =>* qTrigger(false) qConsumed(D:Nat) qChanged(q1, q0, E:Nat)
    qObserved(qExists, q0, false, original, A:Nat)
    qObserved(qEmpty, q0, true, original, B:Nat)
    qObserved(qCountAtLeastTwo, q0, false, original, C:Nat) REST:QCfg
    such that D:Nat < A:Nat /\ D:Nat < B:Nat /\ D:Nat < C:Nat
      /\ E:Nat < A:Nat /\ E:Nat < B:Nat /\ E:Nat < C:Nat .
--- Coverage: two observations in one firing can see DIFFERENT populations.
search [1] in WHIPPLESCRIPT-LIVE-CONTINUATION-QUERY :
  qInit =>* qObserved(qExists, q1, true, original, A:Nat)
    qChanged(q1, q0, B:Nat) qObserved(qEmpty, q0, true, original, C:Nat)
    REST:QCfg such that A:Nat < B:Nat /\ B:Nat < C:Nat .
--- Coverage: a population repair can restore the admission count without
--- restoring trigger presence; this remains a current read, not re-admission.
search [1] in WHIPPLESCRIPT-LIVE-CONTINUATION-QUERY :
  qInit =>* qTrigger(false) qChanged(q1, q0, A:Nat)
    qChanged(q0, q1, B:Nat) qObserved(qExists, q1, true, original, C:Nat)
    REST:QCfg such that A:Nat < B:Nat /\ B:Nat < C:Nat .
--- Coverage: unchanged population retains ordinary predicate results.
search [1] in WHIPPLESCRIPT-LIVE-CONTINUATION-QUERY :
  qUnchanged =>* qObserved(qExists, q1, true, original, A:Nat)
    qObserved(qEmpty, q1, false, original, B:Nat)
    qObserved(qCountAtLeastTwo, q1, false, original, C:Nat) REST:QCfg .
--- Invariant: branch selection agrees with the population AT its observation,
--- regardless of subsequent changes. It does not compare to the final world.
search [1] in WHIPPLESCRIPT-LIVE-CONTINUATION-QUERY :
  qInit =>* qObserved(K:QKind, C:QCount, R:Bool, V:QValue, N:Nat)
    REST:QCfg such that R:Bool =/= qPredicate(K:QKind, C:QCount) .
--- Invariant: a live query never replaces the retained trigger payload.
search [1] in WHIPPLESCRIPT-LIVE-CONTINUATION-QUERY :
  qInit =>* qObserved(K:QKind, C:QCount, R:Bool, later, N:Nat) REST:QCfg .
--- Invariant: within this observation abstraction, false results do not
--- strand a pending branch; no runtime completion claim is made here.
search [1] in WHIPPLESCRIPT-LIVE-CONTINUATION-QUERY :
  qInit =>! qPending(K:QKind) REST:QCfg .
--- Negative control: unchanged admission/current populations cannot disagree,
--- even under the stale-read counterfactual.
search [1] in WHIPPLESCRIPT-STALE-CONTINUATION-QUERY :
  qUnchanged =>* qObserved(K:QKind, C:QCount, R:Bool, V:QValue, N:Nat)
    REST:QCfg such that R:Bool =/= qPredicate(K:QKind, C:QCount) .
--- Bite: stale admission-query evaluation produces a wrong branch result
--- once the independent population changes. The live-read invariant above
--- must fail when its observer is replaced by this counterfactual.
search [1] in WHIPPLESCRIPT-STALE-CONTINUATION-QUERY :
  qInit =>* qObserved(K:QKind, C:QCount, R:Bool, V:QValue, N:Nat)
    REST:QCfg such that R:Bool =/= qPredicate(K:QKind, C:QCount) .
